  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200, multiprofile, and avgpool (config_005) is the clear best at 0.650 acc, while image-only (config_010) is very weak at 0.208. This creates a critical uncertainty: does adding image features to the strong RNA signal provide complementary information, or does the weak image branch dilute performance? This is the single most consequential design decision for the remaining search. Config_030 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the natural extension of the best RNA configuration into the multimodal setting, using the simpler concat fusion to minimize confounding variables. If it matches or beats 0.650, multimodal is a promising direction worth further exploration; if it underperforms, we can confidently rule out the large multimodal sub-space and concentrate budget on RNA-only refinements (e.g., scvi_n200 + transformer in config_006, or other RNA improvements). Resolving this question maximally reduces uncertainty about which branch of the search tree to pursue, making it the highest-information-value experiment under a limited budget."
